    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n19443" root="سر" body-key="s">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَسْرُورٌ</span></b>  <i>Happy,</i> or <i>joyful,</i> or <i>glad;</i> or <i>affected
with</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سُرُور</span> [q. v.]. (S, TA.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  <i>Having the navel-string cut.</i> (TA, from a trad.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  And with <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ة</span>,
applied to the kind of jar termed <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُزَمَّلَة</span>, <i>Having
a</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سُرَّة</span>, meaning a <i>perforation in the middle, in
which is fixed a tube of silver or lead, whence one
drinks.</i> (Har p. 548.)

